        {
          "identifier": "vision:herdr-nexus-v1:L6",
          "text": "# The herdr Nexus"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "vision:herdr-nexus-v1:L8",
          "text": "The herdr Nexus owns every pane. It is the one component that runs herdr; when herdr changes, it changes, and nothing else does. It is built first, because it proves the translator and the CLI alone, and it is kept usable by hand: any flow, or the living, drives a pane through `herdr-nexus 'Prompt.{ … }'`."
        },
        {
          "identifier": "vision:herdr-nexus-v1:L10",
          "text": "## Signal"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "vision:herdr-nexus-v1:L11",
          "text": "The herdr Nexus also observes: a pane's state is read from herdr and pushed to subscribers as it changes, so the Flow Nexus learns a harness has died without a hook. A pane carries a label, the address of the flow in it, so a listing reads as the definition does."
        },
        {
          "identifier": "vision:herdr-nexus-v1:L13",
          "text": "```ethos"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "vision:herdr-nexus-v1:L14",
          "text": "Signal"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "vision:herdr-nexus-v1:L15",
          "text": "[ herdr:[ Session PaneId Pane Workspace"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "vision:herdr-nexus-v1:L16",
          "text": "          Command Text Keys Outcome Label State ] ]"
        },
